{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"43b4b6a1a76bed8c","name":"card_unit_thunder_division","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/NavalWarfare/units/card_unit_thunder_division","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"THUNDER DIVISION","text":"Once per turn, when you play an Intel card, your other units get +2+2.","flavorText":"The 29th Division of the Imperial Japanese Army, known as the Thunder Division, was established in 1941 in Nagoya. It initially served under the Kwantung Army in Manchukuo and included the 18th, 38th, and 50th Infantry Regiments. In 1944, the division was reassigned to the 31st Army and sent to defend the Mariana Islands, anticipating a major US assault. During its transfer, the transport ship Sakito Maru was torpedoed by the submarine USS Trout. Over half of the 18th Infantry Regiment perished in the attack. The surviving troops landed on Guam, joining the rest of the division to prepare defensive positions. From July 21 to August 10, 1944, the Thunder Division fought against US forces in the Battle of Guam. Despite strong fortifications and determined resistance, the division was eventually overwhelmed. The majority of its personnel were killed in the battle.","faction":"Japan","type":"infantry","rarity":"Unique","cost":6,"operationCost":2,"attack":6,"defense":6},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_thunder_division","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_thunder_division_title","SourceString":"THUNDER DIVISION","LocalizedString":"THUNDER DIVISION"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":6,"defense":6,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":6,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_thunder_division_text","SourceString":"Once per turn, when you play an Intel card, your other units get +2+2.","LocalizedString":"Once per turn, when you play an Intel card, your other units get +2+2."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_thunder_division_history","SourceString":"The 29th Division of the Imperial Japanese Army, known as the Thunder Division, was established in 1941 in Nagoya. It initially served under the Kwantung Army in Manchukuo and included the 18th, 38th, and 50th Infantry Regiments. In 1944, the division was reassigned to the 31st Army and sent to defend the Mariana Islands, anticipating a major US assault. During its transfer, the transport ship Sakito Maru was torpedoed by the submarine USS Trout. Over half of the 18th Infantry Regiment perished in the attack. The surviving troops landed on Guam, joining the rest of the division to prepare defensive positions. From July 21 to August 10, 1944, the Thunder Division fought against US forces in the Battle of Guam. Despite strong fortifications and determined resistance, the division was eventually overwhelmed. The majority of its personnel were killed in the battle.","LocalizedString":"The 29th Division of the Imperial Japanese Army, known as the Thunder Division, was established in 1941 in Nagoya. It initially served under the Kwantung Army in Manchukuo and included the 18th, 38th, and 50th Infantry Regiments. In 1944, the division was reassigned to the 31st Army and sent to defend the Mariana Islands, anticipating a major US assault. During its transfer, the transport ship Sakito Maru was torpedoed by the submarine USS Trout. Over half of the 18th Infantry Regiment perished in the attack. The surviving troops landed on Guam, joining the rest of the division to prepare defensive positions. From July 21 to August 10, 1944, the Thunder Division fought against US forces in the Battle of Guam. Despite strong fortifications and determined resistance, the division was eventually overwhelmed. The majority of its personnel were killed in the battle."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::NavalWarfare","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnIntelTriggered","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnBeforeOth